<h2>Executive Summary & Key Highlights</h2>

<p>This course report evaluated the strategic management, operational compliance, quality assurance systems, and manufacturing environment of <strong>ZOT Engineering</strong>—Scotland's largest independent contract manufacturer specializing in high-precision PCB design, electronics assembly (PCBA), and sheet metal fabrication.</p>

<h3>Key Analysis Focus Areas:</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Quad-ISO Integrated Management System (IMS):</strong> Evaluation of ZOT's unified quality system spanning ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D (Aerospace), ISO 13485 (Medical Devices), and ISO 14001 (Environmental).</li>
  <li><strong>High-Reliability Manufacturing:</strong> Analysis of mission-critical electro-mechanical manufacturing, including FDA-approved medical device components and ITAR-compliant defence technology.</li>
  <li><strong>Operational Risk & Security:</strong> Review of PUWER machine safety, COSHH fume extraction, ITAR confidentiality protocols, and Cyber Essentials Plus security frameworks.</li>
  <li><strong>Sustainability & EDI:</strong> Assessment of zero-to-landfill waste segregation and inclusive entry pathways via in-house apprenticeship programs.</li>
</ul>

